Client.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts in total. Between attempts it waits `backoff \u00d7 2^(n-1)`: 0.5s after the first failure and 1s after the second.\n\n- **What gets retried:** only 503. If the third attempt also gets a 503, that error is raised. Other HTTP errors (500, 404, \u2026) and network errors are raised straight away with no retry.\n- **Settings:** two new constructor arguments, `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5`. Existing calls to `WeatherClient(base_url, timeout)` still work unchanged.\n\nI tested it against a real local HTTP server:\n- 503, 503, then 200 \u2192 returned the JSON after 3 requests.\n- 503 three times \u2192 raised a 503 error after 3 requests.\n- 500 \u2192 raised immediately after 1 request.\n\nThe client ignores any `Retry-After` header the server sends; adding support for it wasn't part of the request.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 35026, "requests_cache_write": 177750, "requests_cost_usd": 0.9300512, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1712, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial14", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 86, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:49:12.584907+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 26.03, "t_checker_s": 2.378, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1726, "tokens_cache_read": 35026, "tokens_cache_write": 177750, "toke